 the Consumer Cyclical median (8%).","Its share of sector profits slightly exceeds its share of revenue (1.50x).","It accounts for 0.2% of sector revenue and 0.4% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+25.4% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 377 companies in the universe; the top four hold 26% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 7% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 10% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 36% and a beta of 0.83, it moves roughly with the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $285.8M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 57% in the 2020 crash, 21% in the 2022 bear market and 74% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $637 (margin of safety -1%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 18%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $480 to $854 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: EV/EBITDA 15.6 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 25.8 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 46% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 25 covering analysts target $636 on average, 1% below the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 93% clears the cost of capital of 8.9% by 85pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.47).","It runs a 36% gross margin and converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.30x.","ROE of 41% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 6.9, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.7% over 3 years, 15.0% over 5 years and 12.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 10.2% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 16%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 3.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 23, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 3.3% a year to shareholders (3.3% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 4.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 21,382 employees, each generates about $580K of revenue, 1.5x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 14.9% a year.","That works out to $50K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.8M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":65,"head":"Watch: BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $541.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 59, gates 12/26)","ROIC 93.4% vs WACC 8.9%","Revenue grew 15.0%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.3x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 1% above fair value of $637","EV/EBITDA 15.6x vs sector 11.2x","P/FCF 25.8x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":541.47,"vc":{"base":637.03,"base_src":"dcf","bear":479.99,"bull":854.32,"alt_median":434.14,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.4673,"dispersion":0.1815,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.128